WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.162
So what does the inventory actually read?

2
00:00:02.162 --> 00:00:06.773
On the Microsoft Entra side: the role
definitions, so every row gets a name;

3
00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:11.306
the active assignments, with whether
each one is assigned or activated,

4
00:00:11.306 --> 00:00:15.609
direct or through a group, and when
it ends; the eligible assignments,

5
00:00:15.609 --> 00:00:19.988
with their expiration; and the
members of each role-assignable group.

6
00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:23.445
On the Azure side, two Resource
Manager collections give

7
00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:27.050
active and eligible role
schedules for each scope you name.

8
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.713
Everything is on the stable,
generally available versions.

9
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:32.830
Next, where the tier comes from.
